{{Short description|International football tournament stage}}
{{Use dmy dates|date=May 2018}}
The knockout stage of the [[1966 FIFA World Cup]] was the second and final stage of the competition, following the group stage. The knockout stage began on 23 July with the quarter-finals and ended on 30 July 1966 with the [[1966 FIFA World Cup final|final match]], held at [[Wembley Stadium (1923)|Wembley Stadium]] in [[London]]. The top two teams from each group (eight in total) advanced to the knockout stage to compete in a [[Single-elimination tournament|single-elimination]] style tournament. A match for third place also was played between the two losing teams of the semi-finals.

[[England national football team|England]] won the final 4–2 against [[Germany national football team|West Germany]] for their first, and still only, World Cup title.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.fifa.com/tournaments/archive/worldcup/england1966/index.html |title=Hurst the hero for England in the home of football |website=FIFA.com |archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20131220190138/http://www.fifa.com/tournaments/archive/worldcup/england1966/index.html |archivedate=20 December 2013}}</ref>

